INT8 SageAttention kernels vendored from ComfyKitchen

Source: https://github.com/Comfy-Org/comfy-kitchen, tag v0.2.38
(commit 42081bf9bb5fad3992c1256aab4f01b27cbb5816), files
comfy_kitchen/backends/cuda/sage_attention/{quant_qk_int8.cu, quant_v_int8.cu,
sage_attn_launcher.cu, qk_int_sv_i8_cuda.cuh, attn_utils.cuh, cp_async.cuh,
math.cuh, mma.cuh, numeric_conversion.cuh, permuted_smem.cuh} and
comfy_kitchen/backends/cuda/float_utils.cuh. License: Apache-2.0
(assets/licenses/Apache-2.0.txt).

Jasna's changes: only the bf16-input, bf16-output, unmasked paths are kept
(other dtypes, attention masks, the key-mask preparation kernel and the
paged-decode quantizers are removed, unused float_utils.cuh helpers dropped),
and the three launchers are C++ functions in namespace
jasna_ltx::sage_attention declared in launchers.h instead of extern "C"
exports. The kernels themselves are unchanged and are compiled with
comfy-kitchen's nvcc flags.

